{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-40122","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-45170","text":"Graphonomous × box-and-box — Arithmetic Compliance Review"}]},{"id":"blk-40123","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45171","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-45172","text":" review (no behavior change) · "},{"id":"spn-45173","marks":["bold"],"text":"Kernel:"},{"id":"spn-45174","text":" "},{"id":"spn-45175","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box"},{"id":"spn-45176","text":" v0.8.0 (8 rungs, 97 laws) "},{"id":"spn-45177","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope:"},{"id":"spn-45178","text":" how closely the Graphonomous memory engine (OS-001) already conforms to the [&] governance kernel, rung by rung, and the small set of *additive* naming/wiring changes that would make it explicitly compliant."}]},{"id":"blk-40124","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-45179","text":"TL;DR"}]},{"id":"blk-40125","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45180","text":"Graphonomous is "},{"id":"spn-45181","marks":["bold"],"text":"already structurally isomorphic"},{"id":"spn-45182","text":" to the kernel's load-bearing rungs — it just doesn't *name* them. Its coverage→decision policy is the bridge ("},{"id":"spn-45183","marks":["code"],"text":"feasible ▸ permitted ▸ best"},{"id":"spn-45184","text":"); its coverage score is the axiological semiring; its Wilson intervals are the epistemic rung; its cost cap is the resource rung's affine ledger. The gap is "},{"id":"spn-45185","marks":["bold"],"text":"vocabulary + two small guarantees"},{"id":"spn-45186","text":", not architecture. Nothing here requires a core refactor; every recommendation is additive."}]},{"id":"blk-40126","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-45187","text":"Compliance scorecard"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-40128","spans":[{"id":"spn-45188","text":"Kernel rung"}]},{"id":"blk-40129","spans":[{"id":"spn-45189","text":"Graphonomous implementation"}]},{"id":"blk-40130","spans":[{"id":"spn-45190","text":"Compliance"}]}],"id":"blk-40127","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-40131","spans":[{"id":"spn-45191","text":"1. alethic ("},{"id":"spn-45192","marks":["code"],"text":"value"},{"id":"spn-45193","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-40132","spans":[{"id":"spn-45194","marks":["code"],"text":"Topology.compute_kappa/2"},{"id":"spn-45195","text":", SCC analysis; node confidence"}]},{"id":"blk-40133","spans":[{"id":"spn-45196","text":"✅ ~90% — κ is a first-class Value"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40134","spans":[{"id":"spn-45197","text":"2. axiological ("},{"id":"spn-45198","marks":["code"],"text":"score"},{"id":"spn-45199","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-40135","spans":[{"id":"spn-45200","marks":["code"],"text":"Coverage.weighted_sum/2"},{"id":"spn-45201","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45202","marks":["code"],"text":"Reranker"}]},{"id":"blk-40136","spans":[{"id":"spn-45203","text":"◻ ~60% — weighted sum, not a *named* semiring"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40137","spans":[{"id":"spn-45204","text":"3. deontic (norm/govern)"}]},{"id":"blk-40138","spans":[{"id":"spn-45205","marks":["code"],"text":"Coverage.pick_decision/4"},{"id":"spn-45206","text":" floor gates (act/learn/escalate)"}]},{"id":"blk-40139","spans":[{"id":"spn-45207","text":"◻ ~70% — floor present, "},{"id":"spn-45208","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-45209","text":" veto implicit"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40140","spans":[{"id":"spn-45210","text":"4. temporal (LTL ▸ supervise)"}]},{"id":"blk-40141","spans":[{"id":"spn-45211","text":"consolidation cadence; freshness/staleness decay"}]},{"id":"blk-40142","spans":[{"id":"spn-45212","text":"◻ ~40% — time-aware, no LTL obligations"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40143","spans":[{"id":"spn-45213","text":"5. reflexive (entrenched ring-0)"}]},{"id":"blk-40144","spans":[{"id":"spn-45214","text":"— (no self-amendment surface)"}]},{"id":"blk-40145","spans":[{"id":"spn-45215","text":"✕ out of scope"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40146","spans":[{"id":"spn-45216","text":"6. epistemic (knows ▸ believes)"}]},{"id":"blk-40147","spans":[{"id":"spn-45217","marks":["code"],"text":"Uncertainty.interval/1"},{"id":"spn-45218","text":" (Wilson), "},{"id":"spn-45219","marks":["code"],"text":"BeliefRevision"},{"id":"spn-45220","text":" (AGM)"}]},{"id":"blk-40148","spans":[{"id":"spn-45221","text":"✅ ~95% — strongest rung"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40149","spans":[{"id":"spn-45222","text":"7. strategic (coalition power)"}]},{"id":"blk-40150","spans":[{"id":"spn-45223","text":"— (single-agent; delegated to Deliberatic)"}]},{"id":"blk-40151","spans":[{"id":"spn-45224","text":"✕ out of scope"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40152","spans":[{"id":"spn-45225","text":"8. resource (affine ledger)"}]},{"id":"blk-40153","spans":[{"id":"spn-45226","marks":["code"],"text":"CostTracker.budget_exceeded?/0"},{"id":"spn-45227","text":" ($10/day), "},{"id":"spn-45228","marks":["code"],"text":"Forgetter"},{"id":"spn-45229","text":" LRU+decay"}]},{"id":"blk-40154","spans":[{"id":"spn-45230","text":"◻ ~85% — ledger present"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-40155","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-45231","text":"Rung-by-rung detail (grounded in the code)"}]},{"id":"blk-40156","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-45232","text":"Rung 1 — alethic ("},{"id":"spn-45233","marks":["code"],"text":"value"},{"id":"spn-45234","text":") ✅"}]},{"id":"blk-40157","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45235","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/graphonomous/topology.ex"},{"id":"spn-45236","text":" "},{"id":"spn-45237","marks":["code"],"text":"compute_kappa/2"},{"id":"spn-45238","text":" (line 134) computes the "},{"id":"spn-45239","marks":["bold"],"text":"κ cyclicity invariant"},{"id":"spn-45240","text":" — the same Value-family invariant the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-45241","marks":["code"],"text":"value.mjs"},{"id":"spn-45242","text":" carries (alethic \"what can happen\"). Node confidence scores are the truth-degrees over which Value laws "},{"id":"spn-45243","marks":["code"],"text":"L1–L14"},{"id":"spn-45244","text":" range. "},{"id":"spn-45245","marks":["bold"],"text":"Already compliant"},{"id":"spn-45246","text":"; recommend citing the rung-1 correspondence in the "},{"id":"spn-45247","marks":["code"],"text":"Topology"},{"id":"spn-45248","text":" moduledoc so κ is understood as the alethic Value, not a bespoke metric."}]},{"id":"blk-40158","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-45249","text":"Rung 2 — axiological ("},{"id":"spn-45250","marks":["code"],"text":"score"},{"id":"spn-45251","text":") ◻ → name the semiring"}]},{"id":"blk-40159","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45252","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/graphonomous/coverage.ex"},{"id":"spn-45253","text":" "},{"id":"spn-45254","marks":["code"],"text":"weighted_sum/2"},{"id":"spn-45255","text":" (line 604) computes "},{"id":"spn-45256","marks":["code"],"text":"Σ value × weight"},{"id":"spn-45257","text":" and clamps to "},{"id":"spn-45258","marks":["code"],"text":"[0,1]"},{"id":"spn-45259","text":". That is the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-45260","marks":["bold"],"text":"probability semiring"},{"id":"spn-45261","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-45262","marks":["code"],"text":"⊕ = +"},{"id":"spn-45263","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45264","marks":["code"],"text":"⊗ = ×"},{"id":"spn-45265","text":") from "},{"id":"spn-45266","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box/score.mjs"},{"id":"spn-45267","text":". "},{"id":"spn-45268","marks":["bold"],"text":"Additive recommendation:"},{"id":"spn-45269","text":" document that the coverage score *is* the axiological rung in the probability semiring, and (optionally) expose a tropical ("},{"id":"spn-45270","marks":["code"],"text":"⊕ = min"},{"id":"spn-45271","text":") \"weakest-component\" view alongside the weighted mean — so the engine can answer \"is any coverage component failing?\" the way the kernel's safety floor does, not just \"how good on average?\"."}]},{"id":"blk-40160","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-45272","text":"Rung 3 — deontic (norm/govern) ◻ → make the "},{"id":"spn-45273","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-45274","text":" veto explicit"}]},{"id":"blk-40161","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45275","marks":["code"],"text":"Coverage.pick_decision/4"},{"id":"spn-45276","text":" (line 392) is "},{"id":"spn-45277","marks":["bold"],"text":"the bridge, already implemented"},{"id":"spn-45278","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-40162","kind":"code","language":"text","text":":act  when coverage ≥ floor  AND uncertainty ≤ ceiling  AND risk ≤ ceiling   # feasible ▸ permitted\n:learn when (looser floor)                                                    # permitted, not yet best\n:escalate otherwise                                                           # floor not met"},{"id":"blk-40163","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45279","text":"This is exactly "},{"id":"spn-45280","marks":["code"],"text":"feasible ▸ permitted ▸ best"},{"id":"spn-45281","text":": the conjunctive thresholds are the "},{"id":"spn-45282","marks":["bold"],"text":"un-weakenable safety floor"},{"id":"spn-45283","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-45284","marks":["code"],"text":"decision_confidence/3"},{"id":"spn-45285","text":" (line 409) is the "},{"id":"spn-45286","marks":["bold"],"text":"gradient"},{"id":"spn-45287","text":" that the bridge's "},{"id":"spn-45288","marks":["code"],"text":"best"},{"id":"spn-45289","text":" step optimizes. The one missing guarantee is "},{"id":"spn-45290","marks":["bold"],"text":"`0̲` annihilation"},{"id":"spn-45291","text":": in the kernel, a floor violation *annihilates* the verdict (no amount of gradient can rescue it). Graphonomous approximates this — "},{"id":"spn-45292","marks":["code"],"text":":escalate"},{"id":"spn-45293","text":" is terminal — but the relationship is implicit. "},{"id":"spn-45294","marks":["bold"],"text":"Additive recommendation:"},{"id":"spn-45295","text":" state in the "},{"id":"spn-45296","marks":["code"],"text":"Coverage"},{"id":"spn-45297","text":" moduledoc that a sub-floor signal annihilates to "},{"id":"spn-45298","marks":["code"],"text":":escalate"},{"id":"spn-45299","text":" (the deontic "},{"id":"spn-45300","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-45301","text":"), and add a property test mirroring the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-45302","marks":["code"],"text":"DB2"},{"id":"spn-45303","text":" annihilation law so the guarantee can't silently regress."}]},{"id":"blk-40164","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-45304","text":"Rung 4 — temporal (LTL ▸ supervise) ◻"}]},{"id":"blk-40165","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45305","text":"Freshness/staleness decay ("},{"id":"spn-45306","marks":["code"],"text":"coverage.ex"},{"id":"spn-45307","text":" line 383) and consolidation cadence are time-aware, but there are no explicit LTL obligations (e.g. \"every stored contradiction is *eventually* resolved\"). "},{"id":"spn-45308","marks":["bold"],"text":"Out of scope to add now"},{"id":"spn-45309","text":"; flagged as the natural next rung if temporal guarantees become first-class. Maps to "},{"id":"spn-45310","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box/temporal.mjs"},{"id":"spn-45311","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-45312","marks":["code"],"text":"X"},{"id":"spn-45313","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45314","marks":["code"],"text":"◇"},{"id":"spn-45315","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-40166","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-45316","text":"Rung 6 — epistemic (knows ▸ believes) ✅ strongest"}]},{"id":"blk-40167","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45317","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/graphonomous/uncertainty.ex"},{"id":"spn-45318","text":" "},{"id":"spn-45319","marks":["code"],"text":"interval/1"},{"id":"spn-45320","text":" (line 28) computes "},{"id":"spn-45321","marks":["bold"],"text":"Wilson confidence intervals"},{"id":"spn-45322","text":" over evidence counts, with an explicit "},{"id":"spn-45323","marks":["code"],"text":":no_evidence"},{"id":"spn-45324","text":" bottom — this is the kernel's epistemic rung (S5/KD45 \"knows ▸ believes\") in statistical form. "},{"id":"spn-45325","marks":["code"],"text":"BeliefRevision"},{"id":"spn-45326","text":" implements "},{"id":"spn-45327","marks":["bold"],"text":"AGM"},{"id":"spn-45328","text":" expansion/contraction with "},{"id":"spn-45329","marks":["code"],"text":"contradicts"},{"id":"spn-45330","text":" edges. "},{"id":"spn-45331","marks":["bold"],"text":"Already compliant"},{"id":"spn-45332","text":" at ~95%; recommend naming the "},{"id":"spn-45333","marks":["code"],"text":":no_evidence"},{"id":"spn-45334","text":" case as the epistemic bottom and citing the rung-6 correspondence. This is the rung Graphonomous could claim conformance on today."}]},{"id":"blk-40168","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-45335","text":"Rung 8 — resource (affine ledger) ◻"}]},{"id":"blk-40169","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45336","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/graphonomous/cost_tracker.ex"},{"id":"spn-45337","text":" "},{"id":"spn-45338","marks":["code"],"text":"budget_exceeded?/0"},{"id":"spn-45339","text":" (line 167) enforces a "},{"id":"spn-45340","marks":["code"],"text":"$10/day"},{"id":"spn-45341","text":" cap — an "},{"id":"spn-45342","marks":["bold"],"text":"affine ledger"},{"id":"spn-45343","text":": spend is consumed and cannot go negative past the cap. The "},{"id":"spn-45344","marks":["code"],"text":"Forgetter"},{"id":"spn-45345","text":" (LRU + priority decay) is resource reclamation. This is the kernel's resource rung ("},{"id":"spn-45346","marks":["code"],"text":"resource.mjs"},{"id":"spn-45347","text":", laws "},{"id":"spn-45348","marks":["code"],"text":"C1–C8"},{"id":"spn-45349","text":"). "},{"id":"spn-45350","marks":["bold"],"text":"Additive recommendation:"},{"id":"spn-45351","text":" emit the daily-budget remaining as a resource signal and name it with the resource-rung vocabulary ("},{"id":"spn-45352","marks":["code"],"text":"consume"},{"id":"spn-45353","text":", overspend → "},{"id":"spn-45354","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-45355","text":"), so unattended autonomy degrades gracefully via the same algebra the kernel uses."}]},{"id"